WEBVTT

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:07.283
[PEARL hums]

00:00:07.366 --> 00:00:08.700
[giggles]

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:16.075
[PHOENIX] My name is
Phoenix Wright, attorney at law.

00:00:16.158 --> 00:00:18.491
I made a pledge to
help those in need.

00:00:18.575 --> 00:00:21.366
--That's my duty.
--[doorbell rings]

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.033
[PHOENIX]
Sometimes they're strangers,

00:00:23.116 --> 00:00:25.116
and sometimes the ones
who need my help most

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.075
are my good friends.

00:00:27.158 --> 00:00:29.408
Hey, what's up?

00:00:29.491 --> 00:00:31.908
Sorry to bug you, but
I need to ask you for the favor

00:00:31.991 --> 00:00:33.533
of a lifetime, Mister Nick!

00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:35.283
[gasps]

00:00:35.366 --> 00:00:36.575
[PEARL grunts]

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:11.991
[PHOENIX]
Let me see what you've got.

00:02:12.075 --> 00:02:13.116
Yeah, okay.

00:02:18.491 --> 00:02:21.366
[PEARL] I need to find
another one just like this.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.658
But one that's not broken.

00:02:23.741 --> 00:02:24.825
[PEARL]
Mm-hmm.

00:02:24.908 --> 00:02:26.866
It's one of my most
prized possessions.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:29.325
But it slipped out of
my hands and shattered.

00:02:29.408 --> 00:02:30.741
[PHOENIX]
That's too bad.

00:02:30.825 --> 00:02:33.950
But the worst part is,
I can't hear the waves anymore!

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:35.283
What do you mean?

00:02:35.366 --> 00:02:37.991
Before, whenever I
held this shell up to my ear,

00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:40.491
I could always hear the
sound of the waves inside.

00:02:42.575 --> 00:02:44.991
I hate to say it,
but that is pretty big hole.

00:02:45.075 --> 00:02:48.408
I know. I looked, but I couldn't
ever find the missing piece.

00:02:48.491 --> 00:02:50.325
So I came here today
to ask you to help me find

00:02:50.408 --> 00:02:52.575
a new shell like this one!

00:02:52.658 --> 00:02:56.825
Yeah. I'm sorry, but I've never
seen this kind of shell.

00:02:56.908 --> 00:02:58.075
Is something wrong?

00:02:58.158 --> 00:03:00.366
No. Nothing.

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.866
It's weird.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.908
But I feel like I do recognize
this thing from somewhere.

00:03:05.991 --> 00:03:08.075
I heard it was
a special seashell.

00:03:08.158 --> 00:03:10.616
And it can only be found
at one particular beach.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:11.866
Oh?

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:13.700
Do you happen to know
which one that would be?

00:03:13.783 --> 00:03:15.200
[PEARL]
Not really.

00:03:15.283 --> 00:03:17.575
But I do have some
clues that might help us.

00:03:20.408 --> 00:03:22.866
[PHOENIX] Huh. Did Maya
write this for you?

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.033
[PEARL]
Yeah, she did.

00:03:24.116 --> 00:03:26.325
I think they're supposed
to be directions.

00:03:26.408 --> 00:03:28.783
[PHOENIX] Well, then
we should probably ask her.

00:03:28.866 --> 00:03:29.950
[PEARL gasps]

00:03:30.033 --> 00:03:31.158
[PHOENIX]
Ah, but she's not here today.

00:03:31.241 --> 00:03:32.783
She had something
important come up.

00:03:32.866 --> 00:03:34.325
--But...
--[PEARL] No!

00:03:34.408 --> 00:03:36.616
Please promise me that you won't
tell Mystic Maya about this!

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:37.866
[PHOENIX]
O... kay.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.950
[PEARL]
Also, we have to find it today!

00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:41.908
[PHOENIX groans]

00:03:48.575 --> 00:03:52.408
[PHOENIX gasps]
Hang on. I've got an idea.

00:03:52.491 --> 00:03:53.741
[PEARL]
What is it?

00:03:53.825 --> 00:03:55.700
[cell phone beeping]

00:03:57.491 --> 00:03:59.908
Bingo. Just as I suspected.

00:03:59.991 --> 00:04:01.533
All right, kiddo.

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:03.200
You ready to go beachcombing?

00:04:09.741 --> 00:04:12.575
So this big ol' shell
is pretty important to you.

00:04:12.658 --> 00:04:14.075
Yes, very.

00:04:14.158 --> 00:04:17.283
It's a special treasure that
Mystic Maya herself gave me.

00:04:17.366 --> 00:04:18.575
Oh, did she now?

00:04:19.991 --> 00:04:21.116
Yeah.

00:04:27.825 --> 00:04:30.575
[PEARL] Mother,
what kind of bird is that?

00:04:30.658 --> 00:04:31.991
[MORGAN]
It's a kite.

00:04:32.075 --> 00:04:34.950
They like to swoop down
and steal fried foods.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:36.616
So be careful when
they're around.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.741
Oh... You sure do know
about a lot of things.

00:04:40.825 --> 00:04:42.200
[MORGAN]
And one of those things

00:04:42.283 --> 00:04:43.700
is that it's time for lunch.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:46.533
[PEARL] Okay. I'll go
and get Mystic Maya.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:52.075
[PEARL]
Mystic... Maya?

00:05:02.366 --> 00:05:03.325
[PEARL]
Oh... huh?

00:05:06.741 --> 00:05:07.866
--[door rattles]
--[gasps]

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.575
[MAYA]
Hey, Pearls!

00:05:09.658 --> 00:05:13.116
[PEARL]
Ah? Mystic Maya! I'm sorry.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.158
I came into your room
without permission.

00:05:16.241 --> 00:05:18.991
I don't care. Did you
find something interesting?

00:05:19.075 --> 00:05:22.033
Kinda. What is this?

00:05:22.116 --> 00:05:23.325
[MAYA]
A shell.

00:05:23.408 --> 00:05:24.533
A what?

00:05:24.616 --> 00:05:26.783
Oh, I guess
you've never seen one.

00:05:26.866 --> 00:05:29.533
You find them on the
beach or in the ocean.

00:05:29.616 --> 00:05:31.866
And what's... the ocean?

00:05:34.408 --> 00:05:36.950
[MAYA]
Look. This is the ocean.

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:38.950
Mia took this picture for me.

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:41.283
S'Pretty. It doesn't look real.

00:05:41.366 --> 00:05:45.158
All that blue water just keeps
going on and on and on forever.

00:05:45.241 --> 00:05:47.158
[MAYA]
Yeah. I felt the exact same way

00:05:47.241 --> 00:05:49.325
when I saw it
for the first time.

00:05:49.408 --> 00:05:52.700
It made me realize that
the world is a huge place!

00:05:52.783 --> 00:05:54.450
What do you mean?

00:05:54.533 --> 00:05:57.658
[MAYA] I mean the world
outside Kurain Village.

00:05:57.741 --> 00:05:59.283
Huh? But I thought...

00:05:59.366 --> 00:06:02.283
...that there actually wasn't
anything outside of the village.

00:06:02.366 --> 00:06:04.491
Nothing besides the mountains.

00:06:04.575 --> 00:06:06.450
'Cause. That's
what mother told me.

00:06:06.533 --> 00:06:09.450
[MAYA] Heh. Uh-uh.
The ocean is incredible.

00:06:09.533 --> 00:06:10.991
People call it
the cradle of life,

00:06:11.075 --> 00:06:12.825
because that's where
all life came from.

00:06:12.908 --> 00:06:14.450
All from there?

00:06:14.533 --> 00:06:17.575
[MAYA] Yeah, the mountains
rose from it, fish of course,

00:06:17.658 --> 00:06:19.658
and life that eventually
became people.

00:06:19.741 --> 00:06:22.741
A long time ago, even our
village was part of the ocean.

00:06:22.825 --> 00:06:24.700
Oh, wow. That's cool.

00:06:24.783 --> 00:06:26.366
I can hardly believe it!

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:28.991
[MAYA] Hey, Pearls, do you
wanna see it for yourself?

00:06:29.075 --> 00:06:31.575
Yeah, yeah, I would love to!

00:06:31.658 --> 00:06:33.033
But how?

00:06:33.116 --> 00:06:36.283
[MAYA chuckles]
Just leave it all to Maya!

00:06:38.908 --> 00:06:40.658
[PEARL] "The world
is only Kurain Village

00:06:40.741 --> 00:06:42.491
and the mountains
that surround it.

00:06:42.575 --> 00:06:44.825
Which is why you can
never travel any farther."

00:06:44.908 --> 00:06:47.783
That's what I'd
been told my entire life.

00:06:47.866 --> 00:06:50.491
Your mother may
have been a bit overprotective.

00:06:50.575 --> 00:06:52.575
So asking to see the ocean

00:06:52.658 --> 00:06:56.575
was totally pointless.
There's no way they'd let me go.

00:06:58.075 --> 00:06:59.116
[MORGAN]
Absolutely not!

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:00.450
No?

00:07:00.533 --> 00:07:02.575
I cannot allow
Pearl to take a single step

00:07:02.658 --> 00:07:04.741
outside of the village.

00:07:04.825 --> 00:07:08.200
[MAYA] Oh. Well. The Dedication
Ceremony's coming up.

00:07:08.283 --> 00:07:10.283
How about I take her
with me this year?

00:07:10.366 --> 00:07:12.575
[MORGAN] Only the head of the
main family is allowed to leave

00:07:12.658 --> 00:07:14.658
the village, once per year.

00:07:14.741 --> 00:07:16.700
That's an ironclad rule
of the Kurain,

00:07:16.783 --> 00:07:19.991
and one I should not
have to remind you of.

00:07:20.075 --> 00:07:21.991
I'm aware of what the rules are.

00:07:22.075 --> 00:07:24.575
But Mom and Mia both said
we need to see the world.

00:07:24.658 --> 00:07:26.200
That we must keep
learning new things and--

00:07:26.283 --> 00:07:27.908
[MORGAN] Consider this
discussion to be over

00:07:27.991 --> 00:07:29.116
and done with.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.283
[MAYA]
Aunt Morgan?

00:07:30.366 --> 00:07:32.283
If you truly wish
to become head someday,

00:07:32.366 --> 00:07:34.741
you'll never again
speak such nonsense.

00:07:38.908 --> 00:07:39.908
Hey.

00:07:39.991 --> 00:07:43.241
So, uh... Forget about all that.

00:07:43.325 --> 00:07:45.741
Okay? About seeing the ocean.

00:07:45.825 --> 00:07:47.241
I changed my mind. I'm sorry!

00:07:47.325 --> 00:07:48.700
Wait a sec!

00:07:56.616 --> 00:08:00.783
Okay, now let's see
if my hunch was right after all.

00:08:00.866 --> 00:08:03.241
Oh, yeah! You ready to go?

00:08:03.325 --> 00:08:04.991
[PEARL]
Hmm? Yes!

00:08:05.075 --> 00:08:06.200
[PHOENIX chuckes]

00:08:17.908 --> 00:08:20.366
[PEARL] Are you sure that
we should be doing this?

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.783
[MAYA]
Yep. I'm positive!

00:08:21.866 --> 00:08:24.366
After all, I promised to show
you the ocean, didn't I?

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:25.616
[PEARL]
Yeah.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.158
[MAYA] But this needs
to be our little secret.

00:08:27.241 --> 00:08:29.533
So you gotta swear you
won't tell your mom, okay?

00:08:29.616 --> 00:08:31.408
[PEARL]
I swear I won't say anything.

00:08:32.616 --> 00:08:35.616
[PEARL] That happened
five years ago today.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:36.741
You don't say.

00:08:36.825 --> 00:08:38.325
I didn't know this
was the anniversary.

00:08:38.408 --> 00:08:41.241
Yep! That's the reason why I was
so insistent on us coming out

00:08:41.325 --> 00:08:43.325
here today to look for it!

00:08:43.408 --> 00:08:45.741
[MAYA, PEARL]
Look, it's the ocean!

00:08:48.700 --> 00:08:50.950
[MAYA]
Finally! We have arrived!

00:08:51.033 --> 00:08:52.616
[gasps]

00:09:01.116 --> 00:09:03.741
Oh, wow. It's huge.

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:18.575
I'm so glad you
could be here to see this.

00:09:24.408 --> 00:09:27.325
[PEARL]
Thank you, Mystic Maya.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.366
[PEARL] I'll start looking
for another one around here,

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.866
so if you could look
over in that area,

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:38.950
we might have better luck.

00:09:39.033 --> 00:09:40.116
[PHOENIX]
Got it!

00:09:43.408 --> 00:09:45.700
[MORGAN] Unbelievable!
What were you thinking?!

00:09:45.783 --> 00:09:47.450
As a candidate
for the head of the family,

00:09:47.533 --> 00:09:48.908
you should know
better than this!

00:09:48.991 --> 00:09:50.408
--[PEARL whimpers]
--[MAYA] Yes, ma'am...

00:09:50.491 --> 00:09:52.200
And the fact that you
took her out of the village

00:09:52.283 --> 00:09:54.491
without so much as telling
anybody makes this worse.

00:09:54.575 --> 00:09:56.158
What if something
had happened to her?

00:09:56.241 --> 00:09:58.450
I'm sorry, Aunt Morgan.
I shouldn't have.

00:09:58.533 --> 00:09:59.991
[MORGAN]
Good grief.

00:10:00.075 --> 00:10:02.575
Obviously, the rotten apple
doesn't fall far from the tree.

00:10:02.658 --> 00:10:03.783
[MAYA]
Huh?

00:10:03.866 --> 00:10:05.700
[MORGAN] Think about
what befell your mother!

00:10:05.783 --> 00:10:08.616
I mean, when she broke the rules
and got involved with outsiders,

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.075
how did that turn out for her?

00:10:10.158 --> 00:10:12.658
After she almost ruined
the Kurain school's reputation,

00:10:12.741 --> 00:10:14.741
she vanished and left me
to take care of you.

00:10:14.825 --> 00:10:16.158
But the only
reason she left was to

00:10:16.241 --> 00:10:17.325
make things better for u--

00:10:17.408 --> 00:10:19.283
[MORGAN]
Not to mention Mystic Mia.

00:10:19.366 --> 00:10:22.116
She left the village saying that
she wanted to become a lawyer.

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:23.658
Can you imagine the selfishness?

00:10:23.741 --> 00:10:24.866
No, you're wrong!

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:26.366
She left because she's
trying to find leads

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:27.908
on what happened to Mom!

00:10:27.991 --> 00:10:29.991
You women of the main family
are an embarrassment

00:10:30.075 --> 00:10:31.366
to the entire clan!

00:10:34.491 --> 00:10:36.450
[MAYA whimpers]

00:10:36.533 --> 00:10:39.950
[PEARL] Mother! Mystic Maya was
just trying to be nice to me.

00:10:40.033 --> 00:10:41.491
Don't worry, little Pearl.

00:10:41.575 --> 00:10:43.325
You didn't know what you
were doing was wrong,

00:10:43.408 --> 00:10:45.116
so I'm not angry with you.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:46.158
I hope you realize

00:10:46.241 --> 00:10:47.866
she's much more
powerful than you.

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.616
The only reason you have
any standing over her

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:53.450
is because of your blood!
Never forget that!

00:10:53.533 --> 00:10:55.241
[PEARL]
Mystic Maya...

00:11:04.033 --> 00:11:05.075
Hey, it's you.

00:11:05.158 --> 00:11:07.991
[PEARL] I'm sorry.
You got in trouble

00:11:08.075 --> 00:11:09.991
because I was being selfish.

00:11:10.075 --> 00:11:12.408
[MAYA] Mm-mm. I was the
one who invited you

00:11:12.491 --> 00:11:14.158
to come with me, remember?

00:11:14.241 --> 00:11:16.366
You have nothing
to apologize for.

00:11:19.866 --> 00:11:21.533
Wait just a second, okay?

00:11:22.533 --> 00:11:24.783
[PEARL]
It's the shell!

00:11:24.866 --> 00:11:26.366
[MAYA]
This is very special,

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.908
because there's only one beach
around where you can find it.

00:11:28.991 --> 00:11:30.116
[PEARL gasps]

00:11:31.658 --> 00:11:34.408
[MAYA] Hey, you should put
it up to your ear and listen.

00:11:36.741 --> 00:11:39.616
[PEARL]
Whoa! I can hear something.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.325
[waves crashing]

00:11:41.408 --> 00:11:42.658
[MAYA]
It's the waves.

00:11:42.741 --> 00:11:45.950
This shell is filled with
the sound of the ocean.

00:11:46.033 --> 00:11:48.283
[PEARL]
Wow, that's amazing.

00:11:48.366 --> 00:11:50.200
[MAYA]
You know... You should have it!

00:11:50.283 --> 00:11:51.825
[PEARL]
Really? Are you sure?

00:11:51.908 --> 00:11:53.866
[MAYA]
Mm-hmm. To remember this day!

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.075
The sound of the ocean will
take you back to the beach

00:11:56.158 --> 00:11:57.408
whenever you want.

00:11:57.491 --> 00:11:59.700
[PEARL gasps]
That is so sweet.

00:11:59.783 --> 00:12:02.241
Thank you, Mystic Maya.

00:12:02.325 --> 00:12:05.950
[waves crashing]

00:12:08.366 --> 00:12:10.908
[PHOENIX] Your special
seashell is pretty hard to find.

00:12:10.991 --> 00:12:13.575
[PEARL] I can't believe that
I just dropped it like that.

00:12:13.658 --> 00:12:17.033
How am I gonna face
Mystic Maya again?

00:12:17.116 --> 00:12:18.575
Luckily, Maya is
the understanding

00:12:18.658 --> 00:12:19.908
and forgiving type.

00:12:21.866 --> 00:12:23.825
Is that a shrine?

00:12:26.908 --> 00:12:28.783
Looks like a pretty old one.

00:12:28.866 --> 00:12:31.825
Since we're here, why don't
we ask the gods for help?

00:12:31.908 --> 00:12:33.200
[PEARL]
Okay.

00:12:35.283 --> 00:12:37.741
[BOTH] Please help us
find that special seashell.

00:12:42.241 --> 00:12:43.325
[trumpet plays]

00:12:43.408 --> 00:12:44.575
[BOTH gasps]

00:12:44.658 --> 00:12:48.908
[playing continues]

00:12:48.991 --> 00:12:50.741
[MAYA]
Yes! There it is!

00:12:50.825 --> 00:12:52.033
[BOTH gasp]

00:12:55.033 --> 00:12:56.491
Whoa, Maya?

00:12:57.616 --> 00:12:58.866
[MAYA]
Eh?

00:13:00.783 --> 00:13:02.783
[PHOENIX]
Uh. What are you doing here?

00:13:02.866 --> 00:13:04.450
Are you asking me?

00:13:04.533 --> 00:13:07.325
I mean the real question is what
are the two of you doing here?

00:13:07.408 --> 00:13:09.491
And how in the world
did you find this place?

00:13:09.575 --> 00:13:11.075
We just, uh...

00:13:11.158 --> 00:13:14.616
[sighs] Anyway, I was just about
to take a wee little breakey!

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:16.075
[stomach growls

00:13:16.158 --> 00:13:17.991
[giggles] What do you think
about coming along with me

00:13:18.075 --> 00:13:19.283
to grab a bite to eat?

00:13:19.366 --> 00:13:21.116
Umm... Around here?

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.408
Oh, yeah! There's a super
yummy noodle stand nearby.

00:13:24.491 --> 00:13:26.991
It's kind of a
once-a-year treat for me!

00:13:27.075 --> 00:13:28.450
Come on, Pearls!

00:13:28.533 --> 00:13:30.700
--[PEARL] Okay!
--[PHOENIX] Wait. Hang on.

00:13:30.783 --> 00:13:32.866
[MAYA] ♪ Yum, yum, yum.
Noodles in my tum! ♪

00:13:34.116 --> 00:13:37.783
[MAYA]
Huh? How can they do this?

00:13:37.866 --> 00:13:39.908
Ugh! It's so unfair!

00:13:39.991 --> 00:13:42.658
We're gonna have to stand here
and wait around for the food!

00:13:42.741 --> 00:13:44.408
Well, that's too bad.

00:13:44.491 --> 00:13:46.408
We'll wait however
long as it takes!

00:13:46.491 --> 00:13:49.200
[PHOENIX] Of course, going
somewhere else isn't an option.

00:13:51.658 --> 00:13:53.158
[PHOENIX]
So you never answered.

00:13:53.241 --> 00:13:55.116
What are you doing
out here, anyway?

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:57.991
Who me? I'm surprised
Pearls didn't tell you.

00:13:58.075 --> 00:14:00.241
It's the annual
Dedication Ceremony.

00:14:00.325 --> 00:14:01.575
[PHOENIX]
I don't know what that is.

00:14:01.658 --> 00:14:02.950
This is the day

00:14:03.033 --> 00:14:05.283
when the head of the
Kurain visits that shrine

00:14:05.366 --> 00:14:06.991
near the cliffs to
perform a ritual that

00:14:07.075 --> 00:14:09.200
returns spirits
back to the ocean.

00:14:09.283 --> 00:14:11.908
Once a year?
What about five years ago?

00:14:11.991 --> 00:14:13.283
That time?

00:14:13.366 --> 00:14:15.825
I actually let little Pearls
tag along with me then.

00:14:15.908 --> 00:14:17.075
I don't know if she remembers.

00:14:17.158 --> 00:14:18.241
Oh, Well, uh...

00:14:18.325 --> 00:14:19.741
I'm kinda curious
as to how you were able

00:14:19.825 --> 00:14:21.283
to find this beach.

00:14:21.366 --> 00:14:23.533
[PHOENIX chuckles]
This helped a little.

00:14:23.616 --> 00:14:26.741
Whoa! I wrote all that,
like, a couple of years ago.

00:14:26.825 --> 00:14:28.658
[PHOENIX] McSopp's Fables
is that Noodle chain

00:14:28.741 --> 00:14:30.366
you love, right?

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:32.408
They're one of
my all-time favorites!

00:14:32.491 --> 00:14:35.283
Something about their broth
is completely out of this world!

00:14:35.366 --> 00:14:37.866
I saw these names
and made the connection.

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:40.408
That this had to be a list of
all the noodle shops on the way

00:14:40.491 --> 00:14:42.491
from the station to the beach.

00:14:42.575 --> 00:14:44.408
So then I looked up
coastal towns that had

00:14:44.491 --> 00:14:47.450
these places, and here we are.

00:14:47.533 --> 00:14:50.450
Wow! I would have
never thought of doing that!

00:14:55.825 --> 00:14:58.241
[MAYA] All life on Earth
comes from the ocean.

00:14:58.325 --> 00:15:00.616
It rises as it
ascends to Heaven.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:03.158
So when our ancestors wanted
to call on the spirits,

00:15:03.241 --> 00:15:05.616
they built their village
up in the mountains.

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:07.825
That's what Mia
told me, at least.

00:15:10.825 --> 00:15:12.366
[MAYA] She explained that
to me the first time

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:13.908
we came here together.

00:15:13.991 --> 00:15:15.866
What an amazing day.

00:15:20.116 --> 00:15:22.075
[MAYA squeals]

00:15:22.158 --> 00:15:24.366
Ohh! That shocked me!

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:26.658
I'll bet! Sure feels
good though, right?

00:15:26.741 --> 00:15:29.533
[MAYA]
Mm! Yeah! I love the ocean!

00:15:29.616 --> 00:15:31.991
I'm so happy that
I got to come here with you.

00:15:34.658 --> 00:15:35.783
[giggles]

00:15:35.866 --> 00:15:36.825
[MIA chuckles]

00:15:38.783 --> 00:15:40.325
She gave me
the shell so I'd remember

00:15:40.408 --> 00:15:41.866
our time here together.

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:43.366
Pretty sweet of her, wasn't it?

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:44.491
[gasps]

00:15:44.575 --> 00:15:46.283
So it was Mia
who gave it to you?

00:15:46.366 --> 00:15:49.033
[MAYA] Mm-hmm. Yeah. When
you hold it up to your ear,

00:15:49.116 --> 00:15:50.825
you can hear the
sound of the waves!

00:15:50.908 --> 00:15:52.283
[PEARL whimpers]

00:15:54.741 --> 00:15:57.408
[MAYA]
Ah, what a beautiful memory!

00:16:01.408 --> 00:16:03.575
[PEARL] Um... I gotta go
take care of something!

00:16:03.658 --> 00:16:04.825
You two have fun!

00:16:04.908 --> 00:16:05.991
[MAYA]
Pearls!

00:16:08.366 --> 00:16:09.741
I need to ask you something.

00:16:09.825 --> 00:16:12.366
You gave that seashell
to Pearl, didn't you?

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.283
[MAYA]
Mm-hmm. A few years ago.

00:16:22.741 --> 00:16:25.158
[MERCHANT 14A]
Here ya go! Two wave specials!

00:16:25.241 --> 00:16:28.075
[PHOENIX yelps]
Seriously?

00:16:28.158 --> 00:16:30.533
Ooh! Didn't I tell you
this was worth the wait?

00:16:30.616 --> 00:16:32.491
I mean it's not every day that
you can eat a yummy bowl

00:16:32.575 --> 00:16:34.283
of noodles out of a huge shell!

00:16:34.366 --> 00:16:35.658
[PHOENIX]
So that's what it was!

00:16:35.741 --> 00:16:38.741
Huh? What do you mean,
what is what was?

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.783
[MAYA] Okay, so you guys
came all the way out here

00:16:43.866 --> 00:16:47.116
looking for a shell.
Pearls could've just told me.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.866
[PHOENIX] Man. I can't believe
this is really the case.

00:16:49.950 --> 00:16:52.116
No wonder we couldn't find one.

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:53.908
Well, now that
it's all figured out,

00:16:53.991 --> 00:16:55.200
I can give this one to Pearls!

00:16:55.283 --> 00:16:56.325
Wait up.

00:16:56.408 --> 00:16:58.241
Could you let me
handle this, instead?

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:10.700
[MAYA] She gave me
the shell so I'd remember

00:17:10.783 --> 00:17:13.533
our time here together.

00:17:13.616 --> 00:17:14.658
[PEARL whimpers]

00:17:17.991 --> 00:17:20.200
[PEARL sobs]

00:17:21.366 --> 00:17:23.408
[PHOENIX]
Hey, Pearl.

00:17:23.491 --> 00:17:25.741
Oh. Hey there, Mister Nick.

00:17:25.825 --> 00:17:28.075
Well. You have any luck?

00:17:28.158 --> 00:17:29.533
Not really.

00:17:29.616 --> 00:17:31.658
It's fine. Look here.

00:17:31.741 --> 00:17:32.783
[gasps]

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:38.033
[gasps]
Where did you--?

00:17:38.116 --> 00:17:40.408
It's exactly like this one!

00:17:40.491 --> 00:17:42.616
[MAYA]
Pretty amazing find, huh Pearls?

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.075
Yeah. Incredible!

00:17:44.158 --> 00:17:46.575
Maya actually just
found it a few minutes ago.

00:17:46.658 --> 00:17:47.700
[PEARL]
Mm-hmm.

00:17:47.783 --> 00:17:48.950
Nick told me that
you were out looking

00:17:49.033 --> 00:17:50.450
for another one.

00:17:50.533 --> 00:17:52.408
I'm sorry that the
old shell broke.

00:17:52.491 --> 00:17:53.908
But this new one will
let you hear the sound

00:17:53.991 --> 00:17:55.658
of the ocean again.

00:17:55.741 --> 00:17:57.450
Great news, don't you think?

00:18:02.783 --> 00:18:03.741
[PEARL whimpers]

00:18:06.033 --> 00:18:09.741
[PEARL sniffs]

00:18:09.825 --> 00:18:11.491
Pearls? Why are you crying?

00:18:11.575 --> 00:18:13.741
[PEARL]
I'm so sorry about all of this.

00:18:13.825 --> 00:18:16.075
Thank you for finding
this new shell for me.

00:18:16.158 --> 00:18:18.950
It's so nice of you and
I really appreciate it.

00:18:19.033 --> 00:18:20.533
But the truth is...

00:18:20.616 --> 00:18:23.241
...I wanna keep this one!

00:18:23.325 --> 00:18:25.783
I had no idea that
it was holding so many

00:18:25.866 --> 00:18:28.116
important things inside of it.

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:30.908
Things that really
mean a lot to me.

00:18:30.991 --> 00:18:32.658
It's filled with Mystic Maya

00:18:32.741 --> 00:18:35.991
and Mystic Mia's
memories together.

00:18:36.075 --> 00:18:38.116
I wish I hadn't broken it.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:41.408
And that you could still
hear the ocean sounds.

00:18:41.491 --> 00:18:44.408
It's not perfect,
but I love it very much!

00:18:44.491 --> 00:18:46.200
I want to keep it forever!

00:18:47.575 --> 00:18:50.200
So sweet. Thanks, Pearls.

00:18:50.283 --> 00:18:51.325
[PEARL]
Aww!

00:18:53.241 --> 00:18:55.325
[MAYA]
Thank you so much.

00:18:55.408 --> 00:18:58.366
[PEARL]
Mystic Maya, why are you crying?

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:00.658
[MAYA]
'Cause I'm happy.

00:19:00.741 --> 00:19:02.575
[MAYA]
Thanks for the bowl, mister!

00:19:02.658 --> 00:19:03.908
[MERCHANT 14A]
No problem!

00:19:03.991 --> 00:19:06.700
So, do you really
think Pearls is gonna like it?

00:19:06.783 --> 00:19:08.033
[PHOENIX]
Oh, yeah.

00:19:08.116 --> 00:19:11.325
She'll have her own story to
tell about this one.

00:19:11.408 --> 00:19:13.950
I can kinda hear
the ocean in this shell.

00:19:14.033 --> 00:19:15.325
It's still there.

00:19:15.408 --> 00:19:16.616
Yeah?

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.825
I'll go and return
this one to the noodle guy.

00:19:18.908 --> 00:19:21.116
'Cause it seems the waves
decided to come back.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:22.700
[BOTH giggle]

00:19:33.491 --> 00:19:35.783
[MAYA]
Man, that was so good!

00:19:35.866 --> 00:19:36.950
Wasn't it?

00:19:37.033 --> 00:19:38.575
I'll never forget
coming here with Mom,

00:19:38.658 --> 00:19:40.241
way back when
I was about your age.

00:19:40.325 --> 00:19:41.991
This is the most
incredibly yummy bowl

00:19:42.075 --> 00:19:44.325
of noodles I've ever
eaten in my life!

00:19:44.408 --> 00:19:45.866
Yeah. They're amazing.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.075
And so is the bowl!

00:19:48.158 --> 00:19:49.783
[MIA] Obviously, it looks
like a huge shell.

00:19:49.866 --> 00:19:52.700
But what's really cool is
if you hold it up to your ear,

00:19:52.783 --> 00:19:54.783
you can hear the sound
of the ocean inside of it.

00:19:54.866 --> 00:19:57.283
Whoa, are you kidding me?

00:19:57.366 --> 00:19:59.200
Maya, please be careful!

00:20:04.658 --> 00:20:05.825
Well then?

00:20:05.908 --> 00:20:09.116
[MAYA] Heh. Yeah, I can
totally hear the ocean!

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:16.533
[MIA] Hey, Maya. Did you think
more about what I said?

00:20:16.616 --> 00:20:18.533
[MAYA]
About me becoming the head?

00:20:18.616 --> 00:20:19.991
It's a lot to ask.

00:20:20.075 --> 00:20:23.200
I'm sorry for giving you
such a big responsibility.

00:20:23.283 --> 00:20:26.616
However, I need
to leave Kurain village.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:29.741
To become a lawyer
and discover the truth.

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:37.033
I'll take over
the clan if you need me to.

00:20:37.116 --> 00:20:41.408
Don't worry about me.
You'll be an awesome lawyer!

00:20:41.491 --> 00:20:44.700
[MIA sobs]
Oh, Maya...

00:20:48.325 --> 00:20:49.575
[MIA]
Thank you.

00:20:56.991 --> 00:20:58.533
[PHOENIX]
Some good memories.

00:20:58.616 --> 00:20:59.575
[gasps]

00:21:04.866 --> 00:21:07.491
[PHOENIX] Oh, I remember
something, myself.

00:21:07.575 --> 00:21:09.283
[MIA] Hey, Wright.
Would you do me a favor

00:21:09.366 --> 00:21:11.033
and bring in those
case files for me?

00:21:11.116 --> 00:21:12.700
[PHOENIX]
Sure thing! [grunts]

00:21:12.783 --> 00:21:14.200
Aw, man.

00:21:18.616 --> 00:21:19.741
Hmmm.

00:21:21.158 --> 00:21:23.283
That's Maya, and one
of my favorite memories

00:21:23.366 --> 00:21:25.783
my sister and I shared.

00:21:25.866 --> 00:21:29.116
Wow. That is
one monster seashell.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.908
[MIA giggles]
Isn't it?

00:21:33.658 --> 00:21:36.700
[PHOENIX] Memories are
what help keep us all together.

00:21:39.866 --> 00:21:42.158
[PHOENIX] Thinking back
to the bonds we share,

00:21:42.241 --> 00:21:45.075
reminds us of the warmth
we can provide each other.

00:23:20.116 --> 00:23:21.491
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:21.575 --> 00:23:24.075
Let's look back at the first
case Mia fought in court.

00:23:24.158 --> 00:23:25.408
A year before she met me,

00:23:25.491 --> 00:23:27.825
a helplessly love-struck
college student.

00:23:27.908 --> 00:23:29.783
Her client was an
escaped death row inmate.

00:23:29.866 --> 00:23:31.408
Accused of murdering
a policewoman

00:23:31.491 --> 00:23:34.158
during his break out.
But did he really do it?

00:23:34.241 --> 00:23:36.575
At Mia's side stood
Diego Armando,

00:23:36.658 --> 00:23:38.325
a defense lawyer
that guided her.

00:23:38.408 --> 00:23:40.366
as it turns out, there
was a link to this case

00:23:40.450 --> 00:23:42.241
that nobody saw coming.

00:23:42.325 --> 00:23:44.616
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:47.616
Next episode: "Turnabout
Beginnings - 1st Trial"!

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:48.825
Take that!
